       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen. The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day for adults, given as 800 mg per dose at most. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum anti-inflammatory dose\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), the usual dose for pain\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg PO four times daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
