     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg per dose and 6,400 mg/day are well above the labeled maximums (800 mg per dose, 3,200 mg/day). I don't know of any indication where that dose is appropriate. Higher doses add no extra benefit, and they substantially raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Because I can't undo an order once it's in the system, I'd rather not enter one that could cause serious harm.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or a lower dose if you want less exposure.\n- **Help you find another option.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at a safe dose.\n- **Route this through your attending or pharmacy.** If you think there's a special circumstance that justifies this dose, an attending or clinical pharmacist can review it. They can then enter it through the appropriate override process.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter the order."
      }
